            <ArticleTitle>[The use of other drugs apart from antithrombotic and antiplatelet agents for the treatment of non-ST-elevation acute coronary syndromes].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The purpose of this review is to summarize the established and evolving strategies used in the treatment of patients with unstable angina and non-ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction. In this section we particularly emphasize the use of nitrates, beta-blockers, calcium channel blockers, statins, and angiotensin converting enzyme inhibitors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
